{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-zec-2-1","title":"Zechariah 2:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God, in the care of Jerusalem, sends to measure it. 6 The redemption of Zion. 10 The promise of God's presence.</p>\n<p>lifted. 1:18 a man. 1:16; Eze 40:3,5; 47:4; Re 11:1; 21:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-zec-2-2","title":"Zechariah 2:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Whither. 5:10; Joh 16:5 To. Jer 31:39; Eze 45:6; 48:15-17,30-35; Re 11:1; 21:15-17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-zec-2-3","title":"Zechariah 2:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>the angel. 1:9,13,14,19; 4:1,5; 5:5 and another. 1:8,10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-zec-2-4","title":"Zechariah 2:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>young. Jer 1:6; Da 1:17; 1Ti 4:12 Jerusalem.We learn from Josephus, that Jerusalem actually overflowed with inhabitants, and gradually extended itself beyond its walls, and that Herod Agrippa fortified the new part, called Bezetha.</p>\n<p>1:17; 8:4,5; 12:6; 14:10,11; Isa 33:20; 44:26; Jer 30:18,19; 31:24,27 Jer 31:38-40; 33:10-13; Eze 36:10,11; Mic 7:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-zec-2-5","title":"Zechariah 2:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>a wall. 9:8; Ps 46:7-11; 48:3,12; Isa 4:5; 12:6; 26:1,2; 33:21; 60:18,19 the glory. Ps 3:3; Isa 60:19; Hag 2:7-9; Lu 2:32; Re 21:10,11,23; 22:3-5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-zec-2-6","title":"Zechariah 2:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>ho. Ru 4:1; Isa 55:1 and flee. 7; Ge 19:17; Isa 48:20; 52:11,12; Jer 1:14; 3:18; 31:8; 50:8; 51:6 Jer 51:45,50; 2Co 6:16,17; Re 18:4 spread. De 28:64; Jer 15:4; 31:10; Eze 5:12; 11:16; 12:14,15; 17:21; Am 9:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-zec-2-7","title":"Zechariah 2:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Deliver. Ge 19:17; Nu 16:26,34; Isa 48:20; 52:11; Jer 50:8; 51:6,45; Ac 2:40 Re 18:4 that. Isa 52:2; Mic 4:10 daughter.The Babylonians were vanquished by the Persians, formerly their servants, under Darius Hystaspes, who took Babylon after a siege of twelve months, demolished its walls, and put 300,000 of the inhabitants to death.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-zec-2-8","title":"Zechariah 2:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>After. 4,5; 1:15,16; Isa 60:7-14 sent. 9,11; Isa 48:15,16; Mal 3:1; Joh 14:23,24,26; 15:21-23; 17:18 1Jo 4:9,10,14 the nations. 2Ki 24:2; Jer 50:17,18; 51:34,35; Eze 25:6,7,12,15; 26:2; 35:5 Joe 3:2-8; Am 1:3-5,9,11,13; Ob 1:10-16; Mic 4:11; 5:6; 7:10 Hab 2:8,17; Zep 2:8 for. Ge 20:6; Ps 105:13-15; Ac 9:4; 2Th 1:6 the apple. De 32:10; Ps 17:8; Mt 25:40,45</p>"},{"id":"tsk-zec-2-9","title":"Zechariah 2:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>I will. Isa 10:32; 11:15; 13:2; 19:16 and they. Isa 14:2; 33:1,23; Jer 27:7; Eze 39:10; Hab 2:8,17; Zep 2:9 and ye. 8; 4:9; 6:15; Jer 28:9; Joh 13:19; 16:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-zec-2-10","title":"Zechariah 2:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>and rejoice. 9:9; Ps 47:1-9; 98:1-3; Isa 12:6; 35:10; 40:9; 42:10; 51:11; 52:9,10 Isa 54:1; 61:10; 65:18,19; 66:14; Jer 30:19; 31:12; 33:11 Zep 3:14,15; Php 4:4 lo. 14:5; Ps 40:7; Isa 40:9-11; Mal 3:1 and I. 8:3; Le 26:12; Ps 68:18; Eze 37:27; Zep 3:17; Mt 28:20; Joh 1:14 Joh 14:23; 2Co 6:15,16; Re 2:1; 21:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-zec-2-11","title":"Zechariah 2:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>many. 8:20-23; Ps 22:27-30; 68:29-31; 72:8-11,17; Isa 2:2-5; 11:9,10 Isa 19:24,25; 42:1-4; 45:14; 49:6,7,22,23; 52:10; 60:3-7; 66:19 Jer 16:19; Mal 1:11; Lu 2:32; Ac 28:28; 1Pe 2:9,10; Re 11:15 in that day. 3:10 my people. Ex 12:49 thou. 9; Eze 33:33; Joh 17:21,23,25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-zec-2-12","title":"Zechariah 2:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>inherit. Ex 19:5,6; De 32:9; Ps 82:8; 135:4; Jer 10:16; 51:19 and shall. 1:17; Isa 41:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-zec-2-13","title":"Zechariah 2:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ZEC","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Be. Ps 46:10; Hab 2:20; Zep 1:7; Ro 3:19; 9:20 for. Ps 68:5; 78:65; Isa 26:20,21; 42:13-15; 51:9; 57:5; Zep 3:8 his holy habitation. Heb. the habitation of his holiness. De 26:15; 2Ch 30:27; *marg: Ps 11:4; 68:5; Isa 57:15; 63:15; Jer 25:30</p>"}]}